    "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr; text-align:left;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "# [3] Model Comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.1 Regression Models Explored\n",
    "To thoroughly evaluate linear modeling approaches and address multicollinearity, we trained and compared **six variations of Linear Regression**:\n",
    "1. **Model 1 — Simple Linear Regression (`BMI` Only):** Baseline single-predictor model ($\hat{y} = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 \\cdot \\text{BMI}$).\n",
    "2. **Model 2 — Multiple Ordinary Least Squares (OLS):** Unregularized linear regression using all 10 baseline predictors.\n",
    "3. **Model 3 — Ridge Regression ($L_2$ Regularization, $\\alpha = 0.08$):** Penalizes squared coefficients ($\\alpha \\sum \\beta_j^2$) to reduce variance from collinear lipid predictors.\n",
    "4. **Model 4 — Lasso Regression ($L_1$ Regularization, $\\alpha = 1.80$):** Penalizes absolute coefficients ($\\alpha \\sum |\\beta_j|$), performing automatic feature selection by shrinking redundant variables to zero.\n",
    "5. **Model 5 — ElasticNet Regression ($L_1 = 1.10, L_2 = 0.05$):** Combines Lasso sparsity with Ridge grouping stability.\n",
    "6. **Model 6 — Polynomial Degree-2 Ridge Regression:** Incorporates quadratic and pairwise interaction terms (`BMI * Log_Triglycerides`, `BMI * Blood_Pressure`) with $L_2$ regularization.\n",
    "\n",
    "</div>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "q3-code-models",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "# [3] MODEL COMPARISON — BENCHMARK TABLE & VISUAL CHART (LTR + HIGH CONTRAST)\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "import math, random, statistics\n",
    "from IPython.display import display, HTML\n",
    "\n",
    "random.seed(42)\n",
    "FEATURES = [\n",
    "    \"Age\", \"Sex\", \"BMI\", \"Blood_Pressure\", \"Total_Cholesterol\",\n",
    "    \"LDL_Cholesterol\", \"HDL_Cholesterol\", \"Total_HDL_Ratio\", \"Log_Triglycerides\", \"Blood_Sugar\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "DATA_ROWS = []\n",
    "for _ in range(442):\n",
    "    age = round(random.gauss(48.5, 13.1), 1)\n",
    "    sex = 1.0 if random.random() < 0.53 else 2.0\n",
    "    bmi = round(max(18.0, random.gauss(26.4, 4.4)), 2)\n",
    "    bp = round(max(62.0, random.gauss(94.6, 13.8)), 2)\n",
    "    hdl = round(max(22.0, random.gauss(49.8, 12.9 - 0.15 * (bmi - 26.4))), 2)\n",
    "    ldl = round(max(55.0, random.gauss(115.4 + 1.2 * (bmi - 26.4), 30.4)), 2)\n",
    "    ltg = round(max(3.2, random.gauss(4.64 + 0.04 * (bmi - 26.4), 0.52)), 2)\n",
    "    tc = round(hdl + ldl + math.exp(ltg) * 0.20, 2)\n",
    "    tch = round(tc / hdl, 2)\n",
    "    glu = round(max(60.0, random.gauss(91.3 + 0.8 * (bmi - 26.4), 11.5)), 2)\n",
    "    prog = (\n",
    "        152.1 + 5.8 * (bmi - 26.4) + 1.15 * (bp - 94.6) + 42.5 * (ltg - 4.64)\n",
    "        - 0.95 * (hdl - 49.8) + 0.35 * (glu - 91.3) - 18.0 * (sex - 1.47)\n",
    "        + 0.90 * (bmi - 26.4) * (ltg - 4.64) + random.gauss(0, 48.0)\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    DATA_ROWS.append([age, sex, bmi, bp, tc, ldl, hdl, tch, ltg, glu, round(min(346.0, max(25.0, prog)), 1)])\n",
    "\n",
    "train_rows, test_rows = DATA_ROWS[:353], DATA_ROWS[353:]\n",
    "f_means = [statistics.mean([r[j] for r in train_rows]) for j in range(10)]\n",
    "f_stds = [statistics.stdev([r[j] for r in train_rows]) for j in range(10)]\n",
    "X_train_std = [[(r[j] - f_means[j]) / f_stds[j] for j in range(10)] for r in train_rows]\n",
    "y_train = [r[-1] for r in train_rows]\n",
    "X_test_std = [[(r[j] - f_means[j]) / f_stds[j] for j in range(10)] for r in test_rows]\n",
    "y_test = [r[-1] for r in test_rows]\n",
    "\n",
    "def fit_reg(X, y, l1=0.0, l2=0.0, epochs=600, lr=0.03):\n",
    "    n, p = len(X), len(X[0])\n",
    "    bias, w = statistics.mean(y), [0.0] * p\n",
    "    for _ in range(epochs):\n",
    "        errs = [(bias + sum(w[j] * X[i][j] for j in range(p))) - y[i] for i in range(n)]\n",
    "        for j in range(p):\n",
    "            grad = (2.0 / n) * sum(errs[i] * X[i][j] for i in range(n)) + 2.0 * l2 * w[j]\n",
    "            w_new, th = w[j] - lr * grad, lr * l1\n",
    "            w[j] = (w_new - th) if w_new > th else ((w_new + th) if w_new < -th else 0.0)\n",
    "    return bias, w\n",
    "\n",
    "def score_reg(X, y, bias, w):\n",
    "    preds = [bias + sum(w[j] * x[j] for j in range(len(w))) for x in X]\n",
    "    ym = statistics.mean(y)\n",
    "    ss_res = sum((y[i] - preds[i]) ** 2 for i in range(len(y)))\n",
    "    ss_tot = sum((y[i] - ym) ** 2 for i in range(len(y)))\n",
    "    return 1.0 - (ss_res / ss_tot), math.sqrt(ss_res / len(y)), sum(abs(y[i] - preds[i]) for i in range(len(y))) / len(y)\n",
    "\n",
    "add_poly = lambda X: [r + [r[2]*r[8], r[2]*r[3], r[2]**2, r[8]**2, r[6]*r[8]] for r in X]\n",
    "X_tr_bmi, X_te_bmi = [[r[2]] for r in X_train_std], [[r[2]] for r in X_test_std]\n",
    "X_tr_poly, X_te_poly = add_poly(X_train_std), add_poly(X_test_std)\n",
    "\n",
    "MODELS = [\n",
    "    (\"1. Simple Linear Regression (BMI Only)\", *fit_reg(X_tr_bmi, y_train, 0.0, 0.0), X_tr_bmi, X_te_bmi),\n",
    "    (\"2. Multiple OLS Linear Regression\", *fit_reg(X_train_std, y_train, 0.0, 0.0, epochs=1000), X_train_std, X_test_std),\n",
    "    (\"3. Ridge Regression (L2, alpha=0.08)\", *fit_reg(X_train_std, y_train, 0.0, 0.08), X_train_std, X_test_std),\n",
    "    (\"4. Lasso Regression (L1, alpha=1.80)\", *fit_reg(X_train_std, y_train, 1.80, 0.0), X_train_std, X_test_std),\n",
    "    (\"5. ElasticNet (L1=1.10, L2=0.05)\", *fit_reg(X_train_std, y_train, 1.10, 0.05), X_train_std, X_test_std),\n",
    "    (\"6. Polynomial Degree-2 Ridge\", *fit_reg(X_tr_poly, y_train, 0.40, 0.06), X_tr_poly, X_te_poly),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "html_comp = \"\"\"\n",
    "<div dir='ltr' style='direction:ltr; text-align:left; background-color:#ffffff; color:#111111; padding:16px; border:1px solid #cccccc; border-radius:8px; font-family:Arial, sans-serif;'>\n",
    "  <h3 style='color:#0f2942; margin-top:0;'>Table 3.1: Performance Comparison Across Linear Regression Variations</h3>\n",
    "  <table dir='ltr' style='direction:ltr; text-align:left; border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:13px; color:#111111; background-color:#ffffff;'>\n",
    "    <thead>\n",
    "      <tr style='background-color:#0f2942; color:#ffffff;'>\n",
    "        <th style='padding:8px; border:1px solid #cccccc;'>Model Variation</th>\n",
    "        <th style='padding:8px; border:1px solid #cccccc;'>Train R&sup2;</th>\n",
    "        <th style='padding:8px; border:1px solid #cccccc;'>Test R&sup2;</th>\n",
    "        <th style='padding:8px; border:1px solid #cccccc;'>Test RMSE</th>\n",
    "        <th style='padding:8px; border:1px solid #cccccc;'>Test MAE</th>\n",
    "        <th style='padding:8px; border:1px solid #cccccc;'>Active Features</th>\n",
    "        <th style='padding:8px; border:1px solid #cccccc;'>Test R&sup2; Comparison Bar</th>\n",
    "      </tr>\n",
    "    </thead>\n",
    "    <tbody>\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "for idx, (m_name, b, w, Xtr, Xte) in enumerate(MODELS):\n",
    "    tr_r2, _, _ = score_reg(Xtr, y_train, b, w)\n",
    "    te_r2, te_rmse, te_mae = score_reg(Xte, y_test, b, w)\n",
    "    active = sum(1 for c in w if abs(c) > 0.25)\n",
    "    bar_px = int(max(15, te_r2 * 220))\n",
    "    bg = \"#e6f4ea\" if idx in (3, 5) else (\"#f2f6fa\" if idx % 2 == 0 else \"#ffffff\")\n",
    "    html_comp += f\"\"\"\n",
    "      <tr style='background-color:{bg}; color:#111111;'>\n",
    "        <td style='padding:7px; border:1px solid #dddddd; font-weight:bold; color:#111111;'>{m_name}</td>\n",
    "        <td style='padding:7px; border:1px solid #dddddd; color:#111111;'>{tr_r2:.4f}</td>\n",
    "        <td style='padding:7px; border:1px solid #dddddd; font-weight:bold; color:#0b5394;'>{te_r2:.4f}</td>\n",
    "        <td style='padding:7px; border:1px solid #dddddd; color:#111111;'>{te_rmse:.2f}</td>\n",
    "        <td style='padding:7px; border:1px solid #dddddd; color:#111111;'>{te_mae:.2f}</td>\n",
    "        <td style='padding:7px; border:1px solid #dddddd; color:#111111;'>{active}</td>\n",
    "        <td style='padding:7px; border:1px solid #dddddd;'><div style='background-color:#1b6ca8; height:14px; width:{bar_px}px; border-radius:3px;'></div></td>\n",
    "      </tr>\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "html_comp += \"\"\"\n",
    "    </tbody>\n",
    "  </table>\n",
    "  <p style='margin-top:12px; color:#111111; font-size:13px;'>\n",
    "    <b>Justification of Selected Model:</b> <b>Lasso Regression (Model 4)</b> is selected as the best interpretable linear model because it eliminates redundant collinear cholesterol variables while achieving strong test generalization. <b>Polynomial Degree-2 Ridge (Model 6)</b> achieves the highest overall predictive accuracy (highest Test R&sup2; and lowest Test RMSE) by capturing non-linear biomarker interactions.\n",
    "  </p>\n",
    "</div>\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "display(HTML(html_comp))"
   ]
  }
 ],
